  "title": "Correct complex factor ordering in the bounded-domain metric and gradient",
  "body": "## Problem\n\nFor complex symmetric points whose real and imaginary parts do not commute, `BoundedDomain.inner` places the two inverse metric factors on the wrong sides of the tangent vector. Its result disagrees with the pullback of `UpperHalf.inner` through the existing Cayley transform. The current gradient conversion also uses the same factor on both sides, so it does not represent Euclidean directional derivatives under the metric and changes incorrectly under unitary coordinate transformations. These errors affect actual Riemannian SGD updates.\n\n## Change\n\nWith `A = I - conj(Z) @ Z` and `B = conj(A)`, evaluate the metric as `trace(B^-1 @ U @ A^-1 @ conj(V))` and convert gradients as `sym(B @ grad @ A)`. Keep the symmetric tangent projection and update the formula documentation and the existing bounded-domain test fixture.\n\nThe existing overall normalization is preserved: the bounded-domain metric equals one quarter of the upper-half metric pulled back through the Cayley transform. At the origin the Cayley derivative is `2i`; this change corrects matrix factor ordering without changing that scale.\n\n## Validation\n\nTwenty regression cases cover complex64/complex128, batched and unbatched points, symmetric and ambient Euclidean gradients, real/diagonal controls, and a real `RiemannianSGD` step. Independent checks use the autograd JVP of the Cayley transform, unitary-congruence covariance, and a six-dimensional real tangent-space Gram solve.\n\nOn both Python 3.8 / PyTorch 2.0.1 CPU and Python 3.12 / PyTorch 2.8.0 CPU:\n\n- The unchanged base implementation produces **16 failures and 4 passing controls**, without collection errors or skips.\n- The fix passes all 20 cases. The complete new regression, Siegel-distance, manifold-basic, and Riemannian-SGD modules report **4959 passed, 310 existing skips**.\n- Production and changed-test Ruff checks, `git diff --check`, and the clean-source check pass.\n\n[Baseline and fixed CI results](https://github.com/Afloat16/geoopt/actions/runs/43668091854). The verification workflow is on a separate fork branch and is not included in this PR.\n",
  "prefilled_url": "https://github.com/geoopt/geoopt/compare/master...Afloat16:fix/bounded-domain-metric-gradient-20261115?expand=1&title=Correct%20complex%20factor%20ordering%20in%20the%20bounded-domain%20metric%20and%20gradient&body=%23%23%20Problem%0A%0AFor%20complex%20symmetric%20points%20whose%20real%20and%20imaginary%20parts%20do%20not%20commute%2C%20%60BoundedDomain.inner%60%20places%20the%20two%20inverse%20metric%20factors%20on%20the%20wrong%20sides%20of%20the%20tangent%20vector.%20Its%20result%20disagrees%20with%20the%20pullback%20of%20%60UpperHalf.inner%60%20through%20the%20existing%20Cayley%20transform.%20The%20current%20gradient%20conversion%20also%20uses%20the%20same%20factor%20on%20both%20sides%2C%20so%20it%20does%20not%20represent%20Euclidean%20directional%20derivatives%20under%20the%20metric%20and%20changes%20incorrectly%20under%20unitary%20coordinate%20transformations.%20These%20errors%20affect%20actual%20Riemannian%20SGD%20updates.%0A%0A%23%23%20Change%0A%0AWith%20%60A%20%3D%20I%20-%20conj(Z)%20%40%20Z%60%20and%20%60B%20%3D%20conj(A)%60%2C%20evaluate%20the%20metric%20as%20%60trace(B%5E-1%20%40%20U%20%40%20A%5E-1%20%40%20conj(V))%60%20and%20convert%20gradients%20as%20%60sym(B%20%40%20grad%20%40%20A)%60.%20Keep%20the%20symmetric%20tangent%20projection%20and%20update%20the%20formula%20documentation%20and%20the%20existing%20bounded-domain%20test%20fixture.%0A%0AThe%20existing%20overall%20normalization%20is%20preserved%3A%20the%20bounded-domain%20metric%20equals%20one%20quarter%20of%20the%20upper-half%20metric%20pulled%20back%20through%20the%20Cayley%20transform.%20At%20the%20origin%20the%20Cayley%20derivative%20is%20%602i%60%3B%20this%20change%20corrects%20matrix%20factor%20ordering%20without%20changing%20that%20scale.%0A%0A%23%23%20Validation%0A%0ATwenty%20regression%20cases%20cover%20complex64%2Fcomplex128%2C%20batched%20and%20unbatched%20points%2C%20symmetric%20and%20ambient%20Euclidean%20gradients%2C%20real%2Fdiagonal%20controls%2C%20and%20a%20real%20%60RiemannianSGD%60%20step.%20Independent%20checks%20use%20the%20autograd%20JVP%20of%20the%20Cayley%20transform%2C%20unitary-congruence%20covariance%2C%20and%20a%20six-dimensional%20real%20tangent-space%20Gram%20solve.%0A%0AOn%20both%20Python%203.8%20%2F%20PyTorch%202.0.1%20CPU%20and%20Python%203.12%20%2F%20PyTorch%202.8.0%20CPU%3A%0A%0A-%20The%20unchanged%20base%20implementation%20produces%20**16%20failures%20and%204%20passing%20controls**%2C%20without%20collection%20errors%20or%20skips.%0A-%20The%20fix%20passes%20all%2020%20cases.%20The%20complete%20new%20regression%2C%20Siegel-distance%2C%20manifold-basic%2C%20and%20Riemannian-SGD%20modules%20report%20**4959%20passed%2C%20310%20existing%20skips**.%0A-%20Production%20and%20changed-test%20Ruff%20checks%2C%20%60git%20diff%20--check%60%2C%20and%20the%20clean-source%20check%20pass.%0A%0A%5BBaseline%20and%20fixed%20CI%20results%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FAfloat16%2Fgeoopt%2Factions%2Fruns%2F43668091854).%20The%20verification%20workflow%20is%20on%20a%20separate%20fork%20branch%20and%20is%20not%20included%20in%20this%20PR.%0A",
